an  IEEE 802.1X Authenticator with a suitable backend Authentica‐
tion Server (typically The configuration file consists of  global
parameters  and  domain  specific configuration: IEEE 802.1X‐2004
RADIUS client RADIUS authentication server WPA/IEEE  802.11i  The
following  parameters  are recognized: Interface name.  Should be
set in mode.  Debugging mode: 0 = no, 1 = minimal, 2 = verbose, 3
= msg dumps, 4 = excessive.  Dump file for state information  (on
SIGUSR1).   The pathname of the directory in which creates domain
socket files for communication with frontend programs such  as  A
group  name  or group ID to use in setting protection on the con‐
trol interface file.  This can be set to allow non‐root users  to
access  the  control  interface files.  If no group is specified,
the group ID of the control interface is not modified  and  will,
typically,  be  the group ID of the directory in which the socket
is created.  The following  parameters  are  recognized:  Require
IEEE  802.1X  authorization.   Optional  displayable message sent
with EAP Request‐Identity.  Key lengths for broadcast keys.   Key
